### Payment Microservice API - Sample Requests
### Use with VS Code REST Client extension or IntelliJ HTTP Client

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8081

### ========================================
### PAYMENT ENDPOINTS
### ========================================

### Make a payment with CARD (Success scenario)
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "orderId": "ORDER-001",
    "amount": 350625.00,
    "currency": "LKR",
    "paymentMethod": "CARD",
    "customerId": "CUST-001"
}

###

### High-value payment - step-up authorization hold (>= 1,500,000 LKR)
### First attempt returns status FAILED with a "Bank authorization hold" reason.
### Retry the returned paymentReference and it clears to SUCCESS.
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "orderId": "ORDER-BULK-001",
    "amount": 1800675.00,
    "currency": "LKR",
    "paymentMethod": "CARD",
    "customerId": "CUST-CORP-01"
}

###

### Make a payment with CASH
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "orderId": "ORDER-002",
    "amount": 2500.50,
    "currency": "LKR",
    "paymentMethod": "CASH",
    "customerId": "CUST-002"
}

###

### Make a payment with BANK_TRANSFER
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "orderId": "ORDER-003",
    "amount": 10000.00,
    "currency": "LKR",
    "paymentMethod": "BANK_TRANSFER",
    "customerId": "CUST-003"
}

###

### Make a payment without customerId (optional field)
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "orderId": "ORDER-004",
    "amount": 500.00,
    "currency": "USD",
    "paymentMethod": "CARD"
}

###

### Make a payment - Missing orderId (should return 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "amount": 1500.00,
    "currency": "LKR",
    "paymentMethod": "CARD"
}

###

### Make a payment - Negative amount (should return 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "orderId": "ORDER-005",
    "amount": -100.00,
    "currency": "LKR",
    "paymentMethod": "CARD"
}

### ========================================
### RETRY PAYMENT ENDPOINTS
### ========================================

### Retry payment with different payment method
### NOTE: Replace PAY-XXXXXXXX with actual payment reference from previous request
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments/PAY-XXXXXXXX/retry
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "paymentMethod": "BANK_TRANSFER",
    "reason": "Card declined, trying bank transfer"
}

###

### Retry payment without changing method
### NOTE: Replace PAY-XXXXXXXX with actual payment reference
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments/PAY-XXXXXXXX/retry
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "reason": "Retry after fixing card details"
}

###

### Retry payment with empty body (just retry with same settings)
### NOTE: Replace PAY-XXXXXXXX with actual payment reference
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments/PAY-XXXXXXXX/retry
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{}

###

### Retry non-existent payment (should return 404)
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments/PAY-INVALID123/retry
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{}

### ========================================
### GET PAYMENT DETAILS
### ========================================

### Get payment by reference
### NOTE: Replace PAY-XXXXXXXX with actual payment reference
GET {{baseUrl}}/payments/PAY-XXXXXXXX
Accept: application/json

###

### Get non-existent payment (should return 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/payments/PAY-INVALID123
Accept: application/json

### ========================================
### ACTUATOR ENDPOINTS
### ========================================

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health
Accept: application/json

###

### Application info
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/info
Accept: application/json
